{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "לכן", :translit "lachein", :gloss "therefore"} {:he "מדה במדה", :translit "midah b'midah", :gloss "measure for measure"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "לכן", :b "מדה במדה"}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'measure for measure' is the rabbinic principle of divine retribution, articulated as the standard by which God punishes or rewards (Sotah 8b–9a; Shabbat 105b). Applied to Numbers 20:12, where God tells Moses and Aaron they will not lead Israel into the land, the punishment follows the precise structure of middah k'neged middah.", :sources ["Sotah 8b" "Sotah 9a" "Shabbat 105b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "לכן", :a-value 100, :b "מדה במדה", :b-value 100, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:30:13.309674384Z", :model "glm-5.2"}